From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Support multi-object DRM PRIME descriptors from V4L2 drivers

FFmpegDescToVA assumes every NV12 and YUV420 DRM PRIME descriptor is a single
contiguous dmabuf holding all planes, and reads only objects[0]:

    MOZ_ASSERT(aDesc.nb_objects == 1);
    vaDesc.objects[0].fd = aDesc.objects[0].fd;
    vaDesc.layers[1].offset[0] = offset + uncrop_width * uncrop_height;

That holds for VA-API and Vulkan. It does not hold for V4L2 multiplanar
drivers, which allocate one buffer per plane and export one dmabuf per plane.
Because MOZ_ASSERT compiles out in release builds, the existing code does not
fail loudly: it constructs a descriptor naming only the luma FD, with chroma
offsets pointing past the end of that buffer. EGL then rejects the import, the
surface comes back null, the caller reports a decode error, and
MediaFormatReader converts any decode error from a hardware decoder into
"disable hardware decoding" - so the failure surfaces as silent software
decode rather than as a diagnosable error.

Adds multi-object branches for both formats. The single-object paths are
untouched.

Also relaxes two gates under MOZ_ENABLE_V4L2:

  - The per-codec checks consult gfxVars::Use*HwDecode(), which reflects
    VA-API capability. V4L2 support is probed when the decoder is created, so
    the probe should decide rather than a VA-API-derived variable.

  - The hardware-WebRender requirement exists because VA-API returns DMABuf
    surfaces that only a hardware compositor can import. V4L2-M2M returns
    ordinary buffers and has no such dependency. It also cannot be satisfied:
    the decoder that performs playback is constructed with a null image
    allocator, so the first clause of isHardwareWebRenderUsed is false for it
    regardless of the compositor.

Measured on CIX Sky1 (Mali-G720 / libmali): with these applied and a
DRM_PRIME-capable libavcodec, all three YUV420 planes import successfully and
CreateImageV4L2 returns success for every frame, with no fallback decoder
created. libmali imports single-plane R8 dmabufs and rejects GR88, which is
why the YUV420 three-R8 layout works where the NV12 R8+GR88 layout does not.

STATUS: NOT SUBMITTED UPSTREAM. Playback still terminates with
NS_ERROR_DOM_MEDIA_FATAL_ERR after the first frames, from a point past
everything instrumented so far. The import chain is correct; something
downstream is not. Submitting a media patch that does not produce working
playback would waste review time, so this is held until that is resolved.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoFramePool.cpp
+++ b/dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoFramePool.cpp
@@ -480,7 +480,32 @@
 
   unsigned int offset = aDesc.layers[0].planes[0].offset;
 
-  if (aDesc.layers[0].format == DRM_FORMAT_YUV420) {
+  if (aDesc.layers[0].format == DRM_FORMAT_YUV420 && aDesc.nb_objects == 3) {
+    // Multi-object YUV420: one dmabuf per plane. The contiguous branch below
+    // reads only objects[0] and derives the chroma offsets from the luma
+    // size, which lands past the end of a luma-only buffer.
+    vaDesc.fourcc = VA_FOURCC_I420;
+
+    vaDesc.num_objects = 3;
+    for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
+      vaDesc.objects[i].drm_format_modifier = aDesc.objects[i].format_modifier;
+      vaDesc.objects[i].size = aDesc.objects[i].size;
+      vaDesc.objects[i].fd = aDesc.objects[i].fd;
+    }
+
+    vaDesc.num_layers = 3;
+    for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
+      vaDesc.layers[i].drm_format = DRM_FORMAT_R8;
+      vaDesc.layers[i].num_planes = 1;
+      vaDesc.layers[i].object_index[0] = i;
+      vaDesc.layers[i].offset[0] =
+          aDesc.layers[0].nb_planes > i ? aDesc.layers[0].planes[i].offset : 0;
+      vaDesc.layers[i].pitch[0] =
+          aDesc.layers[0].nb_planes > i && aDesc.layers[0].planes[i].pitch > 0
+              ? (unsigned int)aDesc.layers[0].planes[i].pitch
+              : (i == 0 ? uncrop_width : uncrop_width / 2);
+    }
+  } else if (aDesc.layers[0].format == DRM_FORMAT_YUV420) {
     vaDesc.fourcc = VA_FOURCC_I420;
 
     // V4L2 expresses YUV420 as a single contiguous buffer containing
@@ -507,6 +532,35 @@
     vaDesc.layers[2].offset[0] = offset + uncrop_width * uncrop_height * 5 / 4;
     vaDesc.layers[2].pitch[0] = uncrop_width / 2;
   } else if (aDesc.layers[0].format == DRM_FORMAT_NV12 &&
+             aDesc.nb_layers == 1 && aDesc.nb_objects == 2) {
+    // Multi-object NV12: one dmabuf per plane, which is what V4L2 multiplanar
+    // drivers export. The single-object branch below reads only objects[0] and
+    // derives the chroma offset from the luma stride; here chroma lives in its
+    // own buffer at its own offset, and objects[1] would be dropped entirely.
+    vaDesc.fourcc = VA_FOURCC_NV12;
+
+    vaDesc.num_objects = 2;
+    for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
+      vaDesc.objects[i].drm_format_modifier = aDesc.objects[i].format_modifier;
+      vaDesc.objects[i].size = aDesc.objects[i].size;
+      vaDesc.objects[i].fd = aDesc.objects[i].fd;
+    }
+
+    vaDesc.num_layers = 2;
+    for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
+      vaDesc.layers[i].num_planes = 1;
+      vaDesc.layers[i].object_index[0] = i;
+      vaDesc.layers[i].offset[0] =
+          aDesc.layers[0].nb_planes > i ? aDesc.layers[0].planes[i].offset : 0;
+    }
+    vaDesc.layers[0].drm_format = DRM_FORMAT_R8;    // Y plane
+    vaDesc.layers[0].pitch[0] = yPitch;
+    vaDesc.layers[1].drm_format = DRM_FORMAT_GR88;  // UV plane
+    vaDesc.layers[1].pitch[0] =
+        aDesc.layers[0].nb_planes >= 2 && aDesc.layers[0].planes[1].pitch > 0
+            ? (unsigned int)aDesc.layers[0].planes[1].pitch
+            : uvPitch;
+  } else if (aDesc.layers[0].format == DRM_FORMAT_NV12 &&
              aDesc.nb_layers == 1) {
     vaDesc.fourcc = VA_FOURCC_NV12;
 
--- a/dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp
+++ b/dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp
@@ -899,8 +899,18 @@
                                   layers::LayersBackend::LAYERS_WR) &&
                                  !mImageAllocator->UsingSoftwareWebRender();
   if (!isHardwareWebRenderUsed) {
+#  ifdef MOZ_ENABLE_V4L2
+    // The hardware-WebRender requirement is a VA-API constraint: that path
+    // returns DMABuf surfaces only a hardware compositor can import. V4L2-M2M
+    // returns ordinary buffers and has no such dependency, and the decoder
+    // that performs playback is constructed without an image allocator, so
+    // this test cannot pass for it regardless of the compositor. Fall through
+    // and let the V4L2 probe decide.
+    FFMPEG_LOG("Hardware WebRender is off; continuing for V4L2");
+#  else
     FFMPEG_LOG("Hardware WebRender is off, VAAPI is disabled");
     return true;
+#  endif
   }
 #  endif
   return aDisableHardwareDecoding;
